    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Copyist at the Nautical Library by day, and the finest forger on the Azure coast by night.</strong> Forty-six. CR 1/4.</p><p>He does not call it forgery. He calls it <em>restoration</em>: everything he makes is a faithful copy of something that already exists, and he is very proud that nothing he has ever made has been found out. Shy, apologetic, precise, and frightened of everything except a blank page.</p><p><strong>In the Gull's Job</strong> he makes the replica Pearl \u2014 black glass over a lead core, the setting cast from the museum's own catalogue drawing \u2014 and the party's papers. He was at the Gull's table in the Mermaid's on Day 12 to take the commission, and spent the brawl under it with his satchel. His one condition: nobody hurts Keeper Whitlock, who lets him sketch in the museum for nothing.</p><p><strong>What he needs from the party:</strong> the Pearl's true size and a good look at its setting by dusk on Day 13; see <em>Laying the Job</em>. If the party tells the Gull their samples were lost at the Ford, he makes the docket too.</p><p><em>Sheet derived from the Zoria Weis stat block (CR 1/4, 27 hp) \u2014 kit renamed.</em></p>",
        "public": ""
      },
